  "volume_summary": "This fully rendered August/September 1970 issue of the Swatantra Newsletter presents the party's case for consolidating nationalist and democratic forces against communism, authoritarian government, and what it portrays as the drift of Indira Gandhi's government toward Soviet influence. Its central materials are speeches by Minoo Masani and C. Rajagopalachari at the Swatantra Party General Council in Madras, the unanimously adopted Political Situation resolution, reports on party proceedings, and annexures setting out resolutions on West Bengal, Cambodia, nationalisation, unemployment, land agitation, taxation, steel, and civil liberties.\n\nThe issue combines opposition politics with an organisational programme. It advocates cooperation with democratic parties, while insisting that any alliance preserve constitutional government, secularism, minority rights, private property, and political freedom. It also records campaigns for Fundamental Rights, opposition to preventive detention and state trading, support for farmers and traders, and efforts to expand the party's regional, youth, and grassroots organisation.",
