      "toc_index": 2,
      "author_resolved": "minoo-masani",
      "summary": "In his General Council address, Minoo Masani supports the AICC(O) appeal for consolidating democratic and nationalist forces. He rejects the conventional “Left”–“Right” classification in favour of a constitutional division between those committed to democratic independence and those seeking dictatorship aligned with Moscow or Peking. Masani presents the proposed programme as a pragmatic basis for cooperation among liberals and democratic socialists, while defending negotiation on economic and social questions.\n\nThe address also attacks the cult of Nehru and the persistence of Marxist categories, criticises communist influence in West Bengal and the Union government, and argues that foreign policy, press freedom, civil rights, minority protection, and economic policy all point to the need for a change of government. Masani closes by defending a modern, non-denominational India and urging organisational discipline, youth work, and cooperation without surrendering Swatantra's principles.",
